<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine firm buys 17,000T U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Philippine firm buys 17,000T U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Philippine flour mill bought 17,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat for November shipment, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal, clinched Tuesday night, was for 8,500 tonnes of dark northern spring wheat with a 14 percent protein content at $4.1 per bushel and 8,500 tonnes of western white wheat at $4.0 per bushel,&quot; said one trader.  </p>
<p>Traders said the price did not include freight.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
